  "settingsRowWatch": "Watch Camera Roll",
  "settingsRowWatchGlasses": "Meta glasses photos",
  "@settingsRowWatchGlasses": {
    "description": "Settings > Photos switch under Watch Camera Roll (design G3): whether the automatic scan logs photos taken with Meta glasses (recognized by file name, album or EXIF). Off: they are not offered; photos added on purpose still are. Kept short: the title shares its line with the switch, and 'Include Meta glasses photos' was cut at 390 pt (row_fit_layout_test)."
  },
  "watcherDisclosureTitle": "Photos will be sent to your AI service",
  "watcherDisclosureBody": "While Watch Camera Roll is on, every new photo in your library, plus the photos from the last {days, plural, =1{day} other{{days} days}}, is sent to {provider} — including ones that are not food — so it can tell whether it is a meal. Each photo is one AI request, so a free tier's daily limit can run out during this first catch-up, and on some free tiers (Gemini's, for example) the AI company may use the photos to improve its AI and let people review them; check its terms or turn on billing. You can turn this off any time.",
  "@watcherDisclosureBody": {
    "description": "One-time notice before Watch Camera Roll is first turned on (App Store 5.1.2(i)), shown ABOVE aiConsentBody in the same dialog — which already says the developer receives nothing, so this text does not repeat it. {provider} is the current AI provider's display name, e.g. Gemini or Claude (server). {days} is the lookback window the enable sweeps right away.",
    "placeholders": {
      "provider": {
        "type": "String"
      },
      "days": {
        "type": "int"
      }
    }
  },
  "watcherDisclosureContinue": "Continue",
  "aiConsentTitle": "Allow AI analysis?",
  "@aiConsentTitle": {
    "description": "Consent dialog (App Store 5.1.2(i)) shown before meal data first goes to an AI recipient from a foreground action: picking a photo, a photo shared into the app, Describe or Fix a meal, Leftovers, Test This Provider, Photo Coverage. Asked again for each new recipient."
  },
  "aiConsentUpdateTitle": "What Chopstats sends has changed",
  "@aiConsentUpdateTitle": {
    "description": "Title of the same consent dialog (aiConsentBody, Not now / Allow), asked ONCE on a launch or return to the app when the current recipient was allowed under an older consent text (core/ai_consent.dart aiConsentWordingVersion): the text now also says a photo taken before 4 a.m. carries the day before's meals, which are sent only after Allow. Not now keeps the older permission as it was."
  },
  "aiConsentUpdateLead": "New: a photo taken before 4 a.m. now also carries a short summary of the day before's meals, so leftovers from a late dinner are recognized. Until you allow it, a photo carries only that day's meals; Not now keeps it that way.",
  "@aiConsentUpdateLead": {
    "description": "First paragraph of the aiConsentUpdateTitle dialog, above the camera-roll notice (while Watch Camera Roll is on) and aiConsentBody: names what changed, so the user need not find it in the full text. Must stay true to AppSettings.previousDayLeftoverContext (a version-1 grant sends that day's meals only) and to aiConsentNotNow's label."
  },
  "aiConsentBody": "Chopstats estimates calories with an AI service. If you allow it, Chopstats sends the following to {recipient}:\n• each photo you log, with your dietary profile and a short summary of the other meals logged that day (for a photo taken before 4 a.m., the day before too)\n• leftover photos, with the meal they belong to\n• what you type to describe a meal\n• what you type to fix a meal, with your meals from the last 7 days\n\nChopstats has no server of its own, and its developer never receives any of this. The AI company's own privacy policy and terms apply to what it receives. Nothing is sent until you allow it, and you can stop at any time in Settings.",
  "@aiConsentBody": {
    "description": "Consent dialog body. {recipient} is aiConsentCompany, aiConsentRelayRecipient or aiConsentServerRecipient(NoHost). The list must stay true to what the app sends (photo_pipeline: the day's other meals; nl/executor: handleText (Fix) sends the 7-day window, describeMeal sends no meals; leftover_flow). A change to WHAT it says is sent also bumps aiConsentWordingVersion (core/ai_consent.dart), so a grant given under the older text is asked again (aiConsentUpdateTitle) before the new data goes.",
    "placeholders": {
      "recipient": {
        "type": "String"
      }
    }
  },
  "aiConsentCompany": "{provider, select, gemini{Google (Gemini)} openai{OpenAI} anthropic{Anthropic (Claude)} xai{xAI (Grok)} openrouter{OpenRouter} deepseek{DeepSeek} qwen{Alibaba Cloud (Qwen)} doubao{ByteDance Volcengine (Doubao)} glm{Zhipu AI (GLM)} other{your AI provider}}",
